<article class="env-lemma" id="0D1B">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0D1B">Lemma <span data-tag="0D1B">99.12.2</span>.</a> Assumption and notation as in Lemma <a href="/tag/0D1A" data-tag="0D1A">99.12.1</a>. The transformation $\mathit{Mor}_ B(Z, X) \longrightarrow \mathrm{Hilb}_{Z \times _ B X/B}$ is representable by open immersions. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Let $T$ be a scheme over $B$ and let $Y \subset (Z \times _ B X)_ T$ be an element of $\mathrm{Hilb}_{Z \times _ B X/B}(T)$. Then we see that $Y$ is the graph of a morphism $Z_ T \to X_ T$ over $T$ if and only if $k = \text{pr}_1|_ Y : Y \to Z_ T$ is an isomorphism. By More on Morphisms of Spaces, Lemma <a href="/tag/05XD" data-tag="05XD">76.49.6</a> there exists an open subscheme $V \subset T$ such that for any morphism of schemes $T' \to T$ we have $k_{T'} : Y_{T'} \to Z_{T'}$ is an isomorphism if and only if $T' \to T$ factors through $V$. This proves the lemma. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>